      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "s1",
          "text": "Brown {i5} in a saucepan by bringing it to a boil. After a few minutes, the milk solids will start to toast and turn a gorgeous brown, nutty color. Keep stirring to ensure even browning. Once you see dark brown bits on the bottom, pour into a liquid measuring cup to stop the cooking.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2",
          "text": "Top up {i5} with {i6} until you reach 1 cup total liquid. Let cool to room temperature.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i6",
            "i5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s3",
          "text": "Sift together {i1}, {i2}, {i3}, and {i4}.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i1",
            "i2",
            "i3",
            "i4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s4",
          "text": "In a separate bowl, cream together {i7} and {i8}. Add {i9} and {i10}.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i7",
            "i8",
            "i9",
            "i10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s5",
          "text": "Add the cooled {i5} to the sugar mixture and cream together until well incorporated.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s6",
          "text": "Add {i11} and {i12} to the butter-sugar mixture and beat until combined.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i11",
            "i12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s7",
          "text": "Add the flour mixture in thirds, beating until you don't see a ton of extra flour. It's okay if a little flour remains unincorporated.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i1",
            "i2",
            "i3",
            "i4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s8",
          "text": "Fold in {i13} and {i14} until just combined, finishing the incorporation of any remaining flour.",
          "ingredientRefs": [
            "i13",
            "i14"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s9",
          "text": "For best flavor, scoop the dough onto a baking sheet and chill in the fridge overnight. Alternatively, you can bake immediately.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s10",
          "text": "Bake until the cookies have cracks and crinkles, with a gooey center and crunchy outside.",
